A||||1||northstar87||Very happy with my Northstar||||10||
Z||000000||northstar87||03-27-2001||03:30 PM||||This weekend was so much fun.  I drove over 2000 miles or so to Florida and back to Indiana.  The car ran perfect.  I had the top down for most of the way. (When we got close to Florida.) It was about 80 all weekend.  I even used the air conditioning.  Had a bunch of fun cruising with Lisa in Daytona.  We also had fun in the mountains of West Viginia.  We were cooking around the turns at about 70 or 80.  We were only supposed to be going 55.  Fun!  The only wish I had about my car is a bigger gas tank.  I still got 24 miles per gallon but only have a 10 gallon gas tank.  That is ok.  Thanks to everyone that ran the Florida Daytona Show.  I will be back next year!!  Thanks again!   I will try to post some pics of Lisas car and of mine.  She should have some posted on her site soon.<P>Chris Moore<BR>ASE Master Auto Tech and Auto Instructor||||reg||10
Z||000001||mrfixit58||03-27-2001||06:27 PM||||Chris,<P>I wish I would have had the time to talk to you. I was one of the guys judging your car (The one in the Panama Jack hat). Your car was absolutly beautiful and deserved the "Best Engineered" award. I hope you took the time to fill out an envelope to get the results of the judging. I tried to write comments on the deductions that may help you in future shows. If all goes well, maybe I'll get an opportunity to talk to you at the next show.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
